// CreateRecastWithBodyWithResponse Put a person into a video (motion transfer)
//
// Replace the person in a video with someone else: a saved or preset creator, a photo, or an AI person made from a description. The new person performs every move, expression and mouth shape of the original, on the same beats and cuts, in the same set and light, and the original sound is kept. Optionally give them a new voice, or have them speak another language with the mouth lip-synced.
//
// PRICED UP FRONT. Send `"dry_run": true` and the response is the exact price: the credits the job reserves when it starts, from the job's own pricing. It is an estimate: the real call reserves the same figure and is charged its actual cost, usually within a few percent of it. Nothing runs and nothing is charged on a dry run, except that reading a social post link uses its one lookup.
//
// ASYNC. A real call answers `202` with the job inside and a `Location` to poll (`GET /v1/jobs/{id}`), usually a few minutes. Or name a `callback_url` and the finished job is POSTed to you.
//
